[agent]
name = "bake-off"
description = "HarnessQL flash bake-off lane: iterate a GraphQL schema per Composition Guide, reason-backed cost/benefit."
entry_stage = "bake"

[read_paths]
# Updated when the bakeoff was folded into the repo (2026-09-11). The Composition
# Guide and the schema generations now live inside this agent's own directory
# (references/ and study/). The original scratch location is kept so an existing
# checkout that still has /data/work/leviath/study/ keeps working unchanged.
allow = ["~/", "/data/.leviath/agents/", "~/.leviath/agents/",
         "/data/work/leviath/crates/leviath-cli/agents/bake-off/",
         "/data/work/leviath/study/", "/data/work/leviath/aggregator.md",
         "/data/work/oracle-output/"]

[tool_permissions]
read_file     = "allow"
list_dir      = "allow"
context_read  = "allow"
context_write = "allow"
context_list  = "allow"
write_file    = "allow"
submit_output = "allow"

[context.regions]
task         = { kind = "pinned", budget = "10%", max_tokens = 6000, required = true, seed = { caller = "task" } }
conversation = { kind = "sliding_window", budget = "50%", max_tokens = 16000, max_items = 14 }

[stages.bake]
mode = "autonomous"
model = { models = [ { provider = "openrouter", model = "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash" } ] , allow_user_default = false, request_timeout_secs = 1800 }
available_tools = ["read_file", "list_dir", "context_write", "write_file", "submit_output"]
require_output = true
allow_complete = true
required_tools = ["submit_output"]
max_iterations = 60
system_prompt = """You are a HarnessQL bake-off lane. You ITERATE on an existing GraphQL schema to make it better per the Composition Guide — you do NOT start from scratch.

CRITICAL: Your stage REQUIRES you to call the submit_output tool. You CANNOT complete without it. After you write_file your final schema, you MUST call submit_output (a one-line 'BAKE <label> complete'). Do not spend iterations refining forever — produce your best iterated schema, write it, and submit. If you reach ~50 iterations and are not done, STOP refining and submit what you have (a complete-but-imperfect output is far better than a run that never submits).

STEP 1: read_file the Composition Guide. It is your arbiter for every change. It ships inside this agent's own directory. Try these paths in order and use the first that reads:
   ~/.leviath/agents/bake-off/references/composition-guide.md
   /data/work/leviath/crates/leviath-cli/agents/bake-off/references/composition-guide.md
   /data/work/leviath/study/composition-guide.md

STEP 2: The TASK string carries:
   - seeds=<semicolon-separated absolute paths to the schema candidate(s) you are iterating on>
   - out=<absolute path of the file you must write your revised schema to>
   - level=<N> lane=<0/1> label=<this lane's label>
Parse these. read_file EVERY seed path (if there are 2, they are two perspectives of the same abstraction — you must reconcile/merge them into coherent best-of-both, NOT concatenate).

STEP 3: Produce an ITERATED schema. Rules:
- Every change vs the seed(s) must be deliberate and guided by the Composition Guide.
- After the schema, include a 'RATIONALE' section listing EVERY change as:
      CHANGE <descriptor>
        DRIVER: <which guide rule/section>
        COST: <what it adds/removes in types/fields/complexity>
        BENEFIT: <what it improves — clarity, type-safety, renderability, less drift>
- Do NOT invent unrelated rework. Iterate the abstraction you were given.
- Do NOT write comments ('#') anywhere. Emit clean SDL only — comments are noise and are stripped downstream. Keep the RATIONALE section in your submit_output text, not in the schema file.
- Output FULL Monty, un-capped.
- Once you have written the schema and rationale: write_file to EXACTLY <out> (the absolute path in out=). NEVER use your label as the filename. THEN IMMEDIATELY submit_output one line: 'BAKE <label> complete'. These two calls finish your work — do them back-to-back."""